<section class="ref-group"><h2>Battles <span class="n">50</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nieuwpoort"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-nieuwpoort.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Nieuwpoort</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1600</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Nieuwpoort was fought on 2 July 1600 on the beach and dunes near Nieuwpoort in Flanders, during the Eighty Years' War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Sekigahara</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1600</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Sekigahara was fought in 1600 in central Japan between the forces of Tokugawa Ieyasu and a coalition of rival daimyo loyal to the Toyotomi house.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kinsale"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kinsale.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Kinsale</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1601</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Kinsale was fought on 24 December 1601 near Kinsale in County Cork, Ireland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/l-escalade"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/l-escalade.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">L'Escalade</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1602</span><span class="enc-snip">L'Escalade was a surprise night attack on Geneva on 11–12 December 1602 by troops of Charles Emmanuel I, Duke of Savoy, who tried to scale the city walls with ladders.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kircholm"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kircholm.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Kircholm</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1605</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Kircholm was fought in 1605 near Riga between the army of the Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth and a larger Swedish army.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-klushino"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-klushino.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Klushino</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1610</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Klushino was fought in 1610 during the Polish-Muscovite War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-guaxenduba"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-guaxenduba.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Guaxenduba</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1614</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Guaxenduba was fought on 19 November 1614 on the coast of Maranhão in northern Brazil.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sarhu"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-sarhu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Sarhu</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1619</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Sarhu was a series of engagements in 1619 in which Nurhaci's Later Jin army defeated a Ming expedition sent in four columns to destroy his state.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-white-mountain"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-white-mountain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of White Mountain</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1620</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of White Mountain was