"56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Benburb</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1646</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Benburb was fought on 5 June 1646 in County Tyrone, where the Ulster army of Confederate Ireland under Owen Roe O'Neill routed a Scottish Covenanter army…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-zhovti-vody"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-zhovti-vody.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Zhovti Vody</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1648</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Zhovti Vody was fought in April and May 1648 in central Ukraine, the first major battle of the Khmelnytsky Uprising.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battles-of-guararapes"><span class="enc-name">Battles of Guararapes</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1648–1649</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battles of Guararapes were two battles fought in April 1648 and February 1649 on the Guararapes hills south of Recife in north-eastern Brazil.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dunbar-1650"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-dunbar-1650.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Dunbar (1650)</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1650</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Dunbar was fought on 3 September 1650 near Dunbar in East Lothian, where Oliver Cromwell's English army defeated a larger Covenanter army under David…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-berestechko"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-berestechko.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Berestechko</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1651</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Berestechko was fought from 28 June to 10 July 1651 in Volhynia, in present-day Ukraine, during the Khmelnytsky Uprising.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-samugarh"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-samugarh.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Samugarh</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1658</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Samugarh was fought on 29 May 1658 near Agra between Dara Shikoh, heir of the ailing Mughal emperor Shah Jahan, and his brothers Aurangzeb and Murad Bakhsh.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-konotop"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-konotop.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Konotop</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1659</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Konotop was fought in the summer of 1659 near Konotop in Ukraine, during the Russo-Polish War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ameixial"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-ameixial.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Ameixial</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1663</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Ameixial was fought on 8 June 1663 near Estremoz in the Alentejo, during the Portuguese Restoration War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sack-of-surat"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/sack-of-surat.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sack of Surat</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1664</span><span class="enc-snip">The sack of Surat in 1664 was a raid by the Maratha leader Shivaji on the wealthy Mughal port city of Surat in Gujarat.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mbwila"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-mbwila.jpg" alt="" load